IMPORT prelude

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore) -- section 4, the definitions the rest of the
-- statute book leans on.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CoA1967.txt. The deposit carries amendments up to
-- Act 24 of 2025 in force from 6 May 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS SECTION. A count across the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this
-- repository found 154 Acts that cite the Companies Act, and section 4(1)
-- alone is cited 235 times, the most-cited single provision in the corpus. The
-- Act is about 1.35 million characters; this encoding takes the definitional core
-- (ss 4, 5, 5A, 5B, 6, 7, 7A and 10) and leaves the other 1.3 million alone.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED from section 4(1): about 62 of its roughly 75 defined terms (13 are encoded:
-- corporation, foreign company, company, private company, public company, exempt private
-- company, director, officer, voting share, debenture, listed, constitution and
-- related corporation, the last in coa-groups.l4). They are
-- either cross-references to another Act ("approved exchange", "Depository",
-- "book-entry securities", "public accountant"), plain glossary ("books", "filed",
-- "lodged", "printed", "solicitor", "prescribed") or terms used only by Parts this
-- row does not reach ("annual return", "statutory report", "treasury share",
-- "minimum subscription", "prospectus", "default penalty").

§ `Companies Act 1967 -- section 4`

§§ `4(1) "corporation" and "foreign company" -- two definitions that point at each other`

-- s 4(1): "'corporation' means any body corporate formed or incorporated or
-- existing in Singapore or outside Singapore AND INCLUDES ANY FOREIGN COMPANY but
-- DOES NOT INCLUDE --
--   (a) any body corporate that is incorporated in Singapore and is by
--       notification of the Minister in the Gazette declared to be a public
--       authority or an instrumentality or agency of the Government or to be a
--       body corporate which is not incorporated for commercial purposes;
--   (b) any corporation sole;
--   (c) any cooperative society;
--   (d) any registered trade union;
--   (da) any platform work association registered under the Platform Workers Act
--        2024; or
--   (e) any limited liability partnership."
--
-- s 4(1): "'foreign company' means --
--   (a) a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated
--       outside Singapore; or
--   (b) an UNINCORPORATED society, association or other body which under the law
--       of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of
--       the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed
--       for that purpose and which does not have its head office or principal
--       place of business in Singapore."
--
-- Two things follow from putting those side by side.
--
-- FIRST. "Corporation" includes any foreign company, and foreign company limb (b)
-- takes in bodies that are NOT incorporated. So an unincorporated foreign
-- association that can sue through its secretary is a "corporation" for the whole
-- Act although it is not a body corporate.
--
-- SECOND. Limb (a) of "foreign company" takes in "society" and "association", and
-- exclusion (c) removes "any cooperative society" without qualification. A
-- cooperative society incorporated outside Singapore is therefore both included
-- (as a foreign company) and excluded. The words "but does not include" give the
-- exclusion the last word, and this encoding reads it that way; it is a reading
-- of the text and the Act does not say which prevails.
--
-- Exclusion (a) is the only one confined to bodies incorporated in Singapore.
--
-- MODELLING. The kinds `a cooperative society` and `a limited liability partnership`
-- mean the Singapore bodies. A cooperative society formed abroad is modelled as
-- `a body incorporated outside Singapore` with the `a cooperative society` flag set,
-- and a foreign limited liability partnership as the same kind with the LLP flag
-- left FALSE, because exclusion (e) means 'limited liability partnership' within
-- section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005, which is a body formed
-- under that Act.
DECLARE BodyKind IS ONE OF
    `a company incorporated under this Act`
    `a body corporate formed in Singapore that is not a company`
    `a body incorporated outside Singapore`
    `an unincorporated body with a foreign place of origin that may sue or be sued through its secretary`
    `a corporation sole`
    `a cooperative society`
    `a registered trade union`
    `a platform work association`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `something that is not a body corporate and not a foreign body`

DECLARE Body HAS
    `what it is` IS A BodyKind
    `incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared by the Minister in the Gazette a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or not incorporated for commercial purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a cooperative society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a limited liability partnership within section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(1) "foreign company".
GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a foreign company` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`'s `what it is`
    WHEN `a body incorporated outside Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a cooperative society` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an unincorporated body with a foreign place of origin that may sue or be sued through its secretary`
        THEN NOT `the body`'s `has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Exclusions (a) to (e). Each is stated on the body as it is, and (c) and (e) are
-- unqualified as to where the body was formed.
GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body falls within an exclusion from "corporation"` IF
        (    `the body`'s `incorporated in Singapore`
         AND `the body`'s `declared by the Minister in the Gazette a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or not incorporated for commercial purposes`)
    OR  `the body`'s `what it is` EQUALS `a corporation sole`
    OR  `the body`'s `what it is` EQUALS `a cooperative society`
    OR  `the body`'s `a cooperative society`
    OR  `the body`'s `what it is` EQUALS `a registered trade union`
    OR  `the body`'s `what it is` EQUALS `a platform work association`
    OR  `the body`'s `what it is` EQUALS `a limited liability partnership`
    OR  `the body`'s `a limited liability partnership within section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is within the first limb of "corporation"` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`'s `what it is`
    WHEN `a company incorporated under this Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate formed in Singapore that is not a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body incorporated outside Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a cooperative society` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered trade union` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a platform work association` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a corporation` IF
        (    `the body is within the first limb of "corporation"` `the body`
         OR  `the body is a foreign company` `the body`)
    AND NOT `the body falls within an exclusion from "corporation"` `the body`

§§ `4(1) "company", "private company", "public company", "exempt private company"`

-- s 4(1): "'company' means a company incorporated under this Act or under any
-- corresponding previous written law".
--
-- s 4(1): "'private company' means --
--   (a) any company which immediately prior to 29 December 1967 was a private
--       company under the provisions of the repealed written laws;
--   (b) any company incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18; or
--   (c) any company converted into a private company pursuant to section 31(1),
-- being a company WHICH HAS NOT CEASED TO BE A PRIVATE COMPANY under section 31 or
-- 32."
-- s 4(1): "'public company' means a company OTHER THAN a private company."
--
-- A public company is therefore defined only by exclusion, so a company whose
-- status cannot be traced to limb (a), (b) or (c) is public by default.
DECLARE CompanyStatus HAS
    `incorporated under this Act or a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a private company immediately before 29 December 1967 under the repealed written laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was converted into a private company under section 31(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has since ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the status` IS A CompanyStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is a company` IF
    `the status`'s `incorporated under this Act or a corresponding previous written law`

GIVEN `the status` IS A CompanyStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is a private company` IF
        `the company is a company` `the status`
    AND (    `the status`'s `was a private company immediately before 29 December 1967 under the repealed written laws`
         OR  `the status`'s `was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18`
         OR  `the status`'s `was converted into a private company under section 31(1)`)
    AND NOT `the status`'s `has since ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32`

GIVEN `the status` IS A CompanyStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is a public company` IF
        `the company is a company` `the status`
    AND NOT `the company is a private company` `the status`

-- s 4(1): "'exempt private company' means --
--   (a) a private company in the shares of which NO BENEFICIAL INTEREST is held
--       directly or indirectly BY ANY CORPORATION and which has NOT MORE THAN 20
--       MEMBERS; or
--   (b) any private company, being a private company that is wholly owned by the
--       Government, which the Minister, in the national interest, declares by
--       notification in the Gazette to be an exempt private company."
--
-- THE TWIST IS IN THE WORD "CORPORATION". Limb (a) is defeated by a beneficial
-- interest held by "any corporation", and "corporation" is the defined term with
-- six exclusions. So a private company wholly owned by a cooperative society, a
-- registered trade union, a platform work association, a limited liability
-- partnership, a corporation sole, or a body the Minister has declared a public
-- authority, STILL QUALIFIES, provided it
-- has no more than 20 members. A private company owned by an unincorporated foreign
-- association that can sue through its secretary does NOT qualify, because that
-- association is a "foreign company" and so a "corporation".
DECLARE Shareholder HAS
    `the body` IS A Body
    `holds a beneficial interest in the shares directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE PrivateCompanyFacts HAS
    `the status` IS A CompanyStatus
    `the holders of beneficial interests` IS A LIST OF Shareholder
    `the number of members` IS A NUMBER
    `wholly owned by the Government and declared exempt by the Minister in the Gazette in the national interest` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the holders` IS A LIST OF Shareholder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `some beneficial interest is held by a corporation` IS
    CONSIDER `the holders`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `h` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     (`h`'s `holds a beneficial interest in the shares directly or indirectly`
                  AND `the body is a corporation` (`h`'s `the body`))
             OR  `some beneficial interest is held by a corporation` `rest`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PrivateCompanyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is an exempt private company` IF
        `the company is a private company` (`the facts`'s `the status`)
    AND (    (    NOT `some beneficial interest is held by a corporation` (`the facts`'s `the holders of beneficial interests`)
              AND `the facts`'s `the number of members` AT MOST 20)
         OR  `the facts`'s `wholly owned by the Government and declared exempt by the Minister in the Gazette in the national interest`)

§§ `4(1) "director", "officer", and section 4(2)`

-- s 4(1): "'director' includes any person occupying the position of director of a
-- corporation by whatever name called and includes a person IN ACCORDANCE WITH
-- WHOSE DIRECTIONS OR INSTRUCTIONS the directors or the majority of the directors
-- of a corporation ARE ACCUSTOMED TO ACT and an alternate or substitute director".
--
-- s 4(2): "a person (A) is NOT regarded as a person in accordance with whose
-- directions or instructions the directors ... are accustomed to act BY REASON ONLY
-- that the directors or the majority of the directors act on ADVICE GIVEN BY A IN A
-- PROFESSIONAL CAPACITY."
--
-- So the shadow director is in, and the professional adviser is out, but only by
-- the words "by reason only". An adviser whose advice is in practice always
-- followed AND who is also paid by a major creditor, or who has a seat at the
-- table beyond advice, can still be a director.
--
-- s 4(10): "A reference in this Act to the directors of a company is, in the case
-- of a company which has only one director, to be construed as a reference to that
-- director." s 4(11): and the doing of an act by two or more directors is the doing
-- of it by that director.
DECLARE PersonInRelationToBoard HAS
    `occupies the position of director by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an alternate or substitute director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the directors or a majority of them are accustomed to act on this person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that is by reason only that they act on this person's advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonInRelationToBoard
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a director` IF
        `the person`'s `occupies the position of director by whatever name called`
    OR  `the person`'s `is an alternate or substitute director`
    OR  (    `the person`'s `the directors or a majority of them are accustomed to act on this person's directions or instructions`
         AND NOT `the person`'s `that is by reason only that they act on this person's advice given in a professional capacity`)

-- s 4(10) and (11): with one director the plural is the singular.
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER, `the number of directors who did the act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a requirement that 2 or more directors act is met` IF
        `the number of directors who did the act` AT LEAST 2
    OR  (    `the number of directors of the company` EQUALS 1
         AND `the number of directors who did the act` EQUALS 1)

-- s 4(1): "'officer', in relation to a corporation, includes --
--   (a) any director or secretary of the corporation or a person employed in an
--       executive capacity by the corporation;
--   (b) a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking of the corporation
--       appointed under a power contained in any instrument; and
--   (c) any liquidator of a company appointed in a voluntary winding up,
-- but does not include --
--   (d) any receiver who is not also a manager;
--   (e) any receiver and manager appointed by the Court;
--   (f) any liquidator appointed by the Court or by the creditors; or
--   (g) a judicial manager appointed under Part 7 of the Insolvency, Restructuring
--       and Dissolution Act 2018."
--
-- "Includes" in the opening words makes the list non-exhaustive for the inclusions,
-- and the exclusions are exhaustive in the other direction. A receiver and manager
-- appointed by an instrument is an officer; the same person appointed by the Court
-- is not. A voluntary liquidator is an officer; a liquidator the creditors chose is
-- not.
DECLARE OfficeHeld IS ONE OF
    `a director`
    `the secretary`
    `a person employed in an executive capacity`
    `a receiver and manager appointed under a power in an instrument`
    `a liquidator in a voluntary winding up`
    `a receiver who is not also a manager`
    `a receiver and manager appointed by the Court`
    `a liquidator appointed by the Court`
    `a liquidator appointed by the creditors`
    `a judicial manager under Part 7 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `some other office or none`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN OfficeHeld
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an officer of the corporation` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `a director` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the secretary` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person employed in an executive capacity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a receiver and manager appointed under a power in an instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a liquidator in a voluntary winding up` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4(1) "voting share"`

-- s 4(1): "'voting share', in relation to a body corporate, means an issued share
-- in the body corporate, NOT BEING --
--   (a) a share to which, IN NO CIRCUMSTANCES, is there attached a right to vote; or
--   (b) a share to which there is attached a right to vote ONLY in one or more of
--       the following circumstances:
--       (i) during a period in which a dividend (or part of a dividend) in respect
--           of the share is in arrear;
--       (ii) upon a proposal to reduce the share capital of the body corporate;
--       (iii) upon a proposal that affects rights attached to the share;
--       (iv) upon a proposal to wind up the body corporate;
--       (v) upon a proposal for the disposal of the whole of the property, business
--           and undertakings of the body corporate;
--       (vi) during the winding up of the body corporate."
--
-- A preference share that votes only on its own class rights, on a reduction of
-- capital, on a winding up, or while in arrear is not a voting share. One that votes
-- on anything else, such as the appointment of directors, is.
DECLARE ShareVotingRights HAS
    `is an issued share` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has any right to vote attached in any circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a right to vote in some circumstance other than the six listed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the share` IS A ShareVotingRights
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the share is a voting share` IF
        `the share`'s `is an issued share`
    AND `the share`'s `has any right to vote attached in any circumstances`
    AND `the share`'s `has a right to vote in some circumstance other than the six listed`

§§ `4(1) "debenture", and 4(5), 4(5A)`

-- s 4(1): "'debenture' includes debenture stock, bonds, notes and any other
-- securities of a corporation whether constituting a charge on the assets of the
-- corporation or not, BUT DOES NOT INCLUDE --
--   (a) a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of
--       exchange;
--   (b) subject to the regulations, a PROMISSORY NOTE having a face value of NOT
--       LESS THAN $100,000 and having a maturity period of NOT MORE THAN 12 MONTHS;
--   (c) a prescribed document."
--
-- s 4(5): "any invitation to the public to DEPOSIT MONEY WITH OR LEND MONEY TO a
-- corporation (other than a corporation that is a prescribed entity mentioned in
-- section 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001) is DEEMED to be an
-- invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the corporation."
-- s 4(5A): "any document ... acknowledging or evidencing or constituting an
-- acknowledgment of the indebtedness of the corporation in respect of any money that
-- is or may be deposited with or lent to the corporation in response to such an
-- invitation is DEEMED to be a debenture."
--
-- Read with s 4(1) "borrowing corporation", this is the hook that brings any public
-- deposit-taking within the prospectus regime. The $100,000 promissory-note carve-out
-- needs BOTH a face value of at least $100,000 AND a maturity of no more than 12
-- months.
DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is debenture stock, a bond, a note or another security of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a promissory note` IS A BOOLEAN
    `face value in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `maturity in months` IS A NUMBER
    `is a prescribed document excluded for this provision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `evidences indebtedness for money deposited or lent in response to an invitation to the public` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the promissory note falls within the section 4(1) carve-out` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is a promissory note`
    AND `the instrument`'s `face value in dollars` AT LEAST 100000
    AND `the instrument`'s `maturity in months` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is a debenture` IF
        `the instrument`'s `evidences indebtedness for money deposited or lent in response to an invitation to the public`
    OR  (    `the instrument`'s `is debenture stock, a bond, a note or another security of a corporation`
         AND NOT `the instrument`'s `is a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange`
         AND NOT `the promissory note falls within the section 4(1) carve-out` `the instrument`
         AND NOT `the instrument`'s `is a prescribed document excluded for this provision`)

GIVEN `the invitation was to the public to deposit or lend money` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the corporation is a prescribed entity mentioned in section 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the invitation is deemed an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures` IF
        `the invitation was to the public to deposit or lend money`
    AND NOT `the corporation is a prescribed entity mentioned in section 239(4) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`

§§ `4(1) "listed", and 4(13) -- the memorandum and articles become the constitution`

-- s 4(1): "'listed', in relation to a company or corporation, means a company or
-- corporation that has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in
-- Singapore and HAS NOT BEEN REMOVED from that official list."
GIVEN `admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation is listed` IF
        `admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore`
    AND NOT `removed from that official list`

-- s 4(13): "With effect from 3 January 2016 --
--   (a) the memorandum of association and the articles of association of a company
--       that are in force for the company immediately before that date --
--       (i) are collectively deemed to constitute, and have effect as, that
--           company's constitution; and
--       (ii) may be amended by the company from time to time in the same manner as
--            the constitution of a company; and
--   (b) any reference in any written law and in any contract or other document having
--       legal effect to the memorandum of association, or the articles of association,
--       or both, of a company is deemed to refer to the company's constitution."
--
-- Limb (b) reaches CONTRACTS as well as statutes: a contract signed before 2016 that
-- gives a right "under the articles" now gives it under the constitution.
GIVEN `the company was incorporated before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the memorandum and articles in force on 2 January 2016 are the company's constitution` IF
    `the company was incorporated before 3 January 2016`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a contract that refers to the articles of association now refers to the constitution` IF
    TRUE

§§ `4(3), 4(4) -- statements in lieu of prospectus`

-- s 4(3): "a statement included in a statement in lieu of prospectus is deemed to be
-- untrue if it is MISLEADING IN THE FORM AND CONTEXT in which it is included."
-- s 4(4): a statement is deemed included in a statement in lieu of prospectus "if it
-- is contained in any report or memorandum appearing on the face thereof or by
-- reference incorporated therein or issued therewith."
--
-- Untruth here is not falsity: a literally accurate statement can be "untrue" if the
-- form or context misleads.
GIVEN `the statement is literally false` IS A BOOLEAN, `the statement is misleading in the form and context in which it is included` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is deemed untrue` IF
    `the statement is misleading in the form and context in which it is included`

GIVEN `appears on the face of the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is incorporated into it by reference` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is issued with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report or memorandum is deemed included in the statement in lieu of prospectus` IF
        `appears on the face of the statement in lieu of prospectus`
    OR  `is incorporated into it by reference`
    OR  `is issued with it`

§§ `4(8), 4(9) -- the affairs of a corporation`

-- s 4(8): "A reference in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402 to the
-- affairs of a corporation is, unless the contrary intention appears, to be construed
-- as INCLUDING a reference to -- (a) the promotion, formation, membership, control,
-- business, trading, transactions and dealings ..., property ..., liabilities ...,
-- profits and other income, receipts, losses, outgoings and expenditure of the
-- corporation; (b) for a corporation that is a trustee, the identity of the
-- beneficiaries ...; (c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation;
-- (d) any act or thing done ... while a receiver is in possession, the corporation is
-- under judicial management, a compromise is being administered, or the corporation
-- is being wound up ...; (e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests
-- issued by, the corporation; (f) the power of persons to exercise, or to control the
-- exercise of, the rights to vote attached to shares ...; (g) the persons who are or
-- have been financially interested in the success or failure of the corporation or
-- able to control or materially influence its policy; (h) the circumstances under
-- which a person acquired or disposed of ... shares, debentures or interests; (i)
-- where the corporation has issued interests, the scheme, common enterprise or
-- investment contract to which the interests relate; and (j) matters relating to or
-- arising out of the audit ..."
-- s 4(9): and a reference to the affairs of a company or foreign company is construed
-- as including the affairs of a corporation as so defined.
--
-- The list is introduced by "includes" and so is not exhaustive. The definition is
-- confined by its opening words to eight provisions, and the encoding records that
-- confinement as a function so that a use outside them is visibly outside.
DECLARE ProvisionUsingAffairs IS ONE OF
    `section 8A`
    `section 8C`
    `section 8D`
    `section 216`
    `Part 9`
    `section 402`
    `some other provision`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A ProvisionUsingAffairs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `some other provision` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4(8)(a)-(j), as the categories the subsection names.
DECLARE AffairsCategory IS ONE OF
    `promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, dealings, property, liabilities, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure`
    `who benefits under a trust where the corporation is a trustee`
    `internal management and proceeding`
    `an act done while a receiver, judicial manager, compromise administrator or winding up is in place`
    `ownership of shares, debentures or interests issued by the corporation`
    `power to exercise or control the exercise of votes, or to dispose of or control the disposal of shares`
    `who is or has been financially interested in the corporation's success or failure, or able to control or materially influence its policy`
    `the circumstances in which someone acquired or disposed of shares, debentures or interests`
    `the scheme, common enterprise or investment contract behind interests the corporation has issued`
    `the audit, working papers or auditor's reports`
    `something not on the list`

GIVEN `the category` IS AN AffairsCategory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the category is expressly among the affairs of a corporation` IF
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN `something not on the list` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "Includes" means something not on the list may still be an affair of the
-- corporation. The list cannot be used to show that a matter is outside.
GIVEN `the category` IS AN AffairsCategory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `being absent from the list shows the matter is not an affair of the corporation` IF
    FALSE
